Package: ohmypsh
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Ziya Bayramov <ziya.bayramov.1@yandex.com>
Section: shells
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6
Suggests: git
Homepage: https://github.com/marmeladze/ohmypsh
Description: psh, the pistachio shell - with salt, roast and cage
 A Unix shell written from scratch in C, following the familiar-core
 philosophy: your fingers already know it (pipes, redirects, &&, job
 control, /dev/tcp), but the classic sh traps are fixed - variables
 never word-split, so `rm $file` deletes exactly one file, always.
 .
 Ships with a fish-style line editor (autosuggestions, real-lexer
 syntax highlighting), the oh-my-psh plugin framework (installed to
 /usr/share/psh/omp), and the armory: salt (cat with colors that
 never changes a byte), roast (Markdown rendered for reading), and
 cage (run untrusted commands against a Landlock read-only world).
